//! fail
// The overwrite rule of D17.11 reaches an owning element of an array (D17.7).
// `owners` starts as `{}`, so the store of line 13 finds `owners[0]` empty and
// passes. Nothing empties the element after it, so the store of line 15 is an
// error at its `=`, column 15, in every build mode. The constant index 0 is the
// key of both elements (spec/fir.md 11). A checked build of the same program
// trapped at run time at that position before the rule became static.
// A `del(owners[0])` before line 15 makes the store pass.
// test/overwrite_oracle_test.py holds the position in every mode.
fn main() i32 {
    i32 n = 3;
    i32 mut@ own[2] mut owners = {};
    owners[0] = new(i32, n);
    println(owners[0].len);
    owners[0] = new(i32, n); //! error: cannot prove 'owners[0]' is empty here
    println("unreachable");
    return 0;
}
